==In the manga==
===Pokémon Adventures===
[[File:Lass Pikachu Adventures.png|thumb|150px|A Lass and her Pikachu in [[Pokémon Adventures]]]]
[[File:Ace Trainer Lass Adventures.png|thumb|left|150px|A Lass in the {{MangaArc|X & Y}}]]
====History====
====={{MangaArc|Red, Green & Blue}}=====
A Lass in a Gold, Silver, & Crystal design with her {{p|Pikachu}} made a cameo appearance in ''[[PS039|Just a Spearow Carrier]]'', waiting in line for the [[Indigo Plateau|Indigo]] League.

====={{MangaArc|Gold, Silver & Crystal}}=====
A Lass was seen walking to the [[Indigo Plateau]] in ''[[PS153|Oh, It's Ho-Oh!]]''.

====={{MangaArc|HeartGold & SoulSilver}}=====
In ''[[PS442|Out-Odding Oddish]]'', {{adv|Gold}} accidentally bumped into a Lass with her {{p|Wigglytuff}} while racing to get to the [[Pokéathlon Dome]]. Later in the same chapter, a Lass and her {{p|Meowth}} were seen entering the Pokéathlon Dome.

In ''[[PS446|Weavile Wobbles But It Won't Fall Down]]'', a Lass was shown checking out the Southwest stall at the [[Safari Zone Gate]].

====={{MangaArc|Platinum}}=====
A Lass and her {{p|Pachirisu}} briefly appeared in ''[[PS418|Deprogramming Porygon-Z]]'', where they were waiting in line along with the other Trainers for the opening of the {{OBP|Battle Frontier|Generation IV}}. Later in the same chapter, another Lass was seen encouraging her friend to go with her to the {{OBP|Battle Tower|Generation IV}}.

====={{MangaArc|Black & White}}=====
A Lass along with her {{p|Audino}} was one of the Trainers that was listening to [[Ghetsis]]'s speech in ''[[PS466|An Odd Speech]]''.

In ''[[PS511|Dream a Little Dream]]'', a Lass was briefly seen amongst the Trainers about to enter {{OBP|Victory Road|Black and White}}.

====={{MangaArc|X & Y}}=====
A Lass appeared in ''[[PS554|Kangaskhan...Kangascan't]]'', walking together with a female {{tc|Ace Trainer}} in [[Santalune City]].

===={{MangaArc|Sword & Shield}}====
A Lass was one of [[Leon]]'s onlookers at [[Hammerlocke]] in ''[[PASS17|Stealth!! Infiltrate the Energy Plant]]''.

